From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:44:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 48/76] gdb/linux-nat: don't resume threads to list markers
 without the agent

"info static-tracepoint-markers" let a stopped native program run.

diff --git a/gdb/linux-nat.c b/gdb/linux-nat.c
index 69aa73d2bd4..aabba3763cd 100644
--- a/gdb/linux-nat.c
+++ b/gdb/linux-nat.c
@@ -4351,6 +4351,12 @@ linux_nat_target::static_tracepoint_markers_by_strid (const char *strid)
   ptid_t ptid = ptid_t (pid, 0);
   static_tracepoint_marker marker;
 
+  /* Without the in-process agent there is nobody to ask.  Do not stop
+     and resume the threads for nothing: resuming them would let a
+     program run that the user had stopped.  */
+  if (!agent_loaded_p ())
+    return markers;
+
   /* Pause all */
   target_stop (ptid);
 
